## The short version

**Flic en Flac** is for people who want a long beach and the shortest commute: it is the closest of the west coast villages to Port Louis and Ebène, with a private clinic in the village. **Tamarin** is for people who want a village with surf and dolphins, and two international primary schools within walking or a short driving distance.

## Atmosphere and daily life

Flic en Flac's beach runs for kilometres under filao trees, busy at weekends when Mauritian families come to picnic, relaxed the rest of the week. Tamarin feels more like a village people live in than a resort: Mauritian families, people from abroad who live here all year and the surf community share the same streets.

## The sea

Flic en Flac has a calm lagoon protected by the reef, good for swimming and snorkelling. Tamarin's bay is known for its surf breaks, for experienced surfers, and for the dolphins often seen there early in the morning.

## Schools and healthcare

Tamarin has two international primary schools on the Economic Development Board's list, Paul et Virginie and Telfair. Near Flic en Flac are Westcoast International Primary School at Cascavelle and the secondary school at Medine, and a Middlesex University campus. Clinique de l'Occident is in Flic en Flac; Artemis Cascavelle Hospital is about 5 km from Flic en Flac and 9 km from Tamarin.

## Getting around

From Flic en Flac, Port Louis is about 25 km and Ebène 17 km; from Tamarin, about 29 and 21 km. Rush hour adds a lot to either.

## Our verdict

Commuters and beach lovers: Flic en Flac. Families with young children and surfers: Tamarin. See [Living in Tamarin](/en/areas/tamarin#living) and [Living in Flic en Flac](/en/areas/flic-en-flac#living).

